# Normalise line endings so a file committed on Windows is byte-identical to
# the same file committed on Linux or macOS.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) rewrites LF
# to CRLF in the working tree on every checkout, which makes `git status` dirty
# for files the commit did not touch, and turns warnings like "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" into routine noise you learn to ignore — which is how a real
# diff gets missed.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF as well. The scripts here are run with
# node and sh, and CRLF in a shebang line is a failure mode, so there is no
# platform on which CRLF is the better default for this repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never diff, never convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
